# Seeds for failure cases proptest has generated in the past. It is
# automatically read and these particular cases re-run before any
# novel cases are generated.
#
# It is recommended to check this file in to source control so that
# everyone who runs the test benefits from these saved cases.
#
# Trimmed by hand once: the generated file also held seeds from two
# properties that were themselves wrong (since corrected) and from one that
# was removed, and a seed labelled with a case that was never a bug is worse
# than no seed. All three below are real. In order:
#
# 1. Two devices changing a setting in the same millisecond used not to
#    converge. Named regression test in tests/merge.rs.
# 2. Merge was not idempotent. Collapsing a duplicate removed the row
#    outright, so the second merge of the same copy met an id it had never
#    heard of and adopted it wholesale — the version that had *lost* the
#    tie-break on the first pass. The collapse now leaves a tombstone; see
#    `Vault::dedupe`.
# 3. Not a bug in the code: `merging_a_copy_of_yourself_changes_nothing`
#    claimed more than was true, because a vault built by local edits alone
#    can already hold duplicates. The property was rewritten to say what
#    actually holds. Kept because the shape is a good exercise of it.
